# Mobile Architecture — Layers & Responsibilities

**A layer groups code with one responsibility.** A screen displays information; business rules decide what an operation means; data-access code communicates with services. Separating them lets developers change and test one responsibility without rewriting the others.

Use this page to decide **where a file belongs, what it may call, and what it must not import**. The same boundaries apply to Android, iOS, and React Native. React Native is preferred for new applications; follow the assigned stack for an existing app.

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Examples use synthetic chicken-order data. Keep enterprise endpoints, SDK contracts, credentials, personal data, and sensitive diagnostics in approved systems.

## 1. See the layers first

Our documented structure separates **UI, Domain, Repository, and Data**. Application composition connects their implementations. The repository includes a **contract in the domain** and an **implementation outside the domain**; it is not two network services.

