## 9. Follow one order from tap to result

<MermaidZoom title="Place a chicken order — request out, mapped result back">

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant VIEW as View
    participant VM as ViewModel / Redux State Owner
    participant USE as Domain Use Case
    participant REPO as Repository Implementation
    participant API as Data API Adapter
    participant SERVER as Backend

    VIEW->>VM: User taps Place Order
    VM->>VM: Enter submitting and block overlapping taps
    VM->>USE: Submit current account/request and quantity
    USE->>USE: Validate input
    Note over USE: Invalid input returns without an API call
    USE->>REPO: Submit through OrderRepository contract
    REPO->>API: Execute the approved request
    API->>SERVER: Request order processing
    SERVER-->>API: Return response when available
    API-->>REPO: Decoded response or transport outcome
    REPO->>REPO: Map into domain outcome
    REPO-->>USE: Return outcome
    USE-->>VM: Return result
    VM->>VM: Reject stale account/request results
    VM-->>VIEW: Publish current UI state
```

</MermaidZoom>

| Situation | Primary owner | Expected behavior |
|---|---|---|
| Invalid quantity | Domain, with presentation feedback | No repository submission for that validation path. |
| Repeated tap while pending | Presentation state owner | No overlapping submission through the retained owner. |
| Confirmed response | Repository mapping and state owner | Show only a valid result for the current request/account. |
| Lost response after dispatch | Data/repository classification and recovery owner | Preserve unknown outcome; reconcile before another write. |
| Logout or account switch | Session/composition and state owner | Invalidate old UI work and coordinate unresolved operations. |
| Process ends | Approved durable recovery design | In-memory guards are insufficient; do not assume the order failed. |

Local validation and request IDs do not replace backend authorization or server idempotency. Example quantities 1–20 and fake order `order-001` are teaching values, not confirmed product/API requirements.

